      "writtenOn": "2025-01-20T09:30:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Returning a list here is fine, but it makes it hard to extend the response later (in a backwards compatible way) in case we want to include additional information.\n\nMaybe better define a ValidationOptionsInfo class, that contains a field with the list of plugin push options, and return it here. Then it\u0027s easy to add further fields to it later if needed.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "03f17fbee2e095e7bf9c50a9f14a82e8c74553ce",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6b106f8_12a1aaae",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/plugins/GetValidationOptions.java",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-20T09:30:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the interface that represents the extension internally, we should not return it in the REST API, but rather define a ValidationOptionInfo class in the \u0027com.google.gerrit.extensions.common\u0027 package to control how plugin push options are represented in JSON.\n\nAlso from the naming it\u0027s confusing that the GetValidationOptions returns PluginPushOption\u0027s.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 39,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 48
      },
